    <section>
      <title outputclass="chapter_sub-titles">Early Innovations in Technology</title>
      <p>In the 20th century, the high-tech industry was defined by breakthroughs in computing, telecommunications, and semiconductors. Key milestones like the invention of the transistor, the first computer networks, and the development of microprocessors laid the foundation for the digital age.</p>
