    <section>
      <title outputclass="chapter_sub-titles">Sustainability in Hi-Tech Product Design</title>
      <p>As the world shifts towards sustainability, the tech industry is innovating to reduce its environmental impact. From energy-efficient hardware to eco-friendly manufacturing processes, companies are integrating green technologies into product design to minimize e-waste and power consumption.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <title outputclass="chapter_sub-titles">Environmental Impact of Tech Products</title>
      <p>While high-tech products like smartphones and laptops offer immense utility, they also contribute to electronic waste (e-waste) and energy consumption. The industry is increasingly focused on recycling, energy-efficient components, and sustainable materials to mitigate environmental impact.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <title outputclass="chapter_sub-titles">Transition to Green Technologies</title>
      <p>To tackle environmental challenges, tech companies are investing in renewable energy sources, sustainable manufacturing, and circular economy practices. Innovations in solar-powered devices, low-energy processors, and recyclable materials are examples of the industry's shift to green technologies.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <title outputclass="chapter_sub-titles">The Shift Toward Smart Devices</title>
      <p>Smart devices are at the forefront of the tech revolution, with innovations like Internet of Things (IoT), wearable tech, and connected ecosystems transforming daily life. These devices are designed to enhance productivity, health, and convenience while minimizing environmental impact through energy efficiency.</p>
    </section>
